      "note": "Replaced the non-standard hour numerals (yinyali, yitathu-va-yivali, …) with the standard Umbundu series mosi, vali, tatu, kwãla, tãlo, epandu, epanduvali, ecelãla, ecea, ekwi, ekwi la mosi, ekwi la vali (confident in the series). Patterns are additive 'ohola {h} la <minutes>' using 'la' (and) as in 'ekwi la mosi', tens 'akũi avali/atatu/akwãla/atãlo', half '{h} la oñali' (reusing the locale's half word). Doubts: whether hours take a concord/ordinal ('ohola yavali'); whether 'la' vs 'na' is right here; 'oñali' as half is inherited unverified."
